-- title:
--   From HTo G Closeness Of IP Avg Context
-- statement:
--   **Averaged inner-product differences are controlled by averaged operator distance.**
--
--   Let $\psi$ be a normalized bipartite quantum state, let $\mathcal D$ be a distribution on questions whose stored total weight is at most one, and let $A$ and $B$ be question-indexed operator families with finite outcome set $\mathcal O_A$. Let $C(q,a,b)$ be a second question- and outcome-indexed operator family, with $b$ ranging over a finite set $\mathcal O_B$. Assume
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal D}
--   \left[\sum_{a\in\mathcal O_A}
--   \operatorname{ev}_{\psi}\!\left((A_{q,a}-B_{q,a})^{\dagger}(A_{q,a}-B_{q,a})\right)\right]
--   \le\gamma,
--   $$
--
--   and
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal D}\left[\sum_{a\in\mathcal O_A}
--   \operatorname{ev}_{\psi}\!\left(C_{q,a}C_{q,a}^{\dagger}\right)\right]\le1,
--   \qquad C_{q,a}:=\sum_{b\in\mathcal O_B}C(q,a,b).
--   $$
--
--   Then
--
--   $$
--   \left|\mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal D}\sum_{a,b}\operatorname{ev}_{\psi}(C(q,a,b)A_{q,a})
--   -\mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal D}\sum_{a,b}\operatorname{ev}_{\psi}(C(q,a,b)B_{q,a})\right|
--   \le\sqrt{\gamma}.
--   $$
--
--   The estimate is used in the adjacent-stage move comparisons after the half-sandwich families have been placed in a common context.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_closenessOfIP_avgContext`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
